      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "On the basis of material evidence,\nboth oral and documentary and on hearing the submissions of learned counsel for both parties, the tribunal awarded compensation of Rs.3,97,000/- with interest @ 6% p.a. from the date of petition till depos"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "c17f1ce2442745be9746cfe5de79aba9_41",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "7. Now coming to the aspect of age, avocation and income, it is stated that age of the claimant was 33 years as on the date of occurrence of accident."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "2f1066356abd4171a641663e6d8bc40b_42",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The tribunal taken the income of Rs.10,000/- per month, in view of there being no proof of income."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "b51eef5a8d6c4882ab600217cbf42b4d_43",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "However, the notional income chart of the Legal Services Authority prescribes the income of Rs.12,500/- for the accident year 2018."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "cbbaaad21fa64e60ba4b3b5eee755d89_44",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Accordingly,\nincome is taken as Rs.12,500/-."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "a46d6432c0894688b76c5de0a31ef3cf_45",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The tribunal has rightly applied the multiplier at '16', which does not call for interference."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "7eecc8bd8eb54e34b74b531c44d19bb1_46",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n8. PW.2-Doctor has assessed the disability at 66% to the both upper limbs and 22% to the whole body, whereas, the tribunal not accepting the version of PW.2- NC: 2024:KHC:5004 Doctor,\nadopted the disability at 10% without there being any b"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "ca5e04591b4c486a867910aebf53055b_47",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "I am in agreement with the learned counsel for appellant-claimant that unless there is contra material evidence placed on record to dispute the evidence of PW.2-Doctor, the tribunal, in normal circumstances, should not disturb the disabilit"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "9634730bb2f149c7b3e0798d7b54405d_48",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Of course, the tribunal is at liberty and discretion to assess the functional disability and physical disability or retained the same as expressed by PW.2- Doctor, unless contra material is placed, which is cogent enough to accept the said "
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "30a56190ca34458797be13893cb85880_49",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Hence, the disability in the present case will have Girish @ Mudalagiriyappa vs Anandakumar on 6 February, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/50755120/\n3 to be taken at 22%.\n9."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "b66a82b19c2b4988a9398166d71e4cf8_51",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Since no material is placed on record to show firstly he is a Carpenter and secondly, the disability to the extent of 20% to the whole body, it does NC: 2024:KHC:5004 not warrant interference."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "1294339c18b142d2b37f45de9324b12b_52",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
